{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": [
    "THE single definition of every alert type. Read at RUNTIME by the backend,",
    "the Discord bot and (via GET /api/dashboard/alert-catalog) the dashboard.",
    "",
    "Read at runtime, not compiled in, on purpose: a git pull updates this file",
    "whether or not anything rebuilt. A stale dist used to mean the API rejected",
    "keys the dashboard offered, which surfaced as bad_request on every save.",
    "",
    "Naming rule: the key names the AGENCY, the suffix names the stream.",
    "So qfd/qfd_warning and dfes/dfes_warning, never qld_*/wa_*.",
    "",
    "archiveSource is the data_history `source` value and is deliberately",
    "many-types-to-one: the five Victorian agencies all carry vic_emergency.",
    "The logs page groups by archiveSource; Discord alerts key on `key`."
  ],

  "severityScales": {
    "fire": ["advice", "watch_and_act", "emergency"],
    "bom": ["minor", "moderate", "major"],
    "event": ["minor", "moderate", "major"]
  },

